ils of the countries from which these Indians were brought\nback; and\n(d) the State-wise details of the rescued Indians?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)]\n(a) to (d) The Government of India has accorded the highest priority to\nensure  the  safety  and  well-being  of  Indian  nationals  abroad.  As  per\ninformation available in the Ministry, the number of Indians who were\nstranded in foreign countries, and have been rescued and brought back\nduring the period April 2014 to December 2017 by the Indian Government\nfrom countries affected by war, internal strife and natural disasters, is\n1,01,336.  This figure also includes repatriation of Indian nationals from\nabroad  for  various  other  reasons  including  those  caught  in  situations,\nimpacted by economic slowdown in the Gulf region and facing difficulty\ndue to employment related issues.  Details are given at Annexure.\n*****\n\nANNEXURE\nS.\n N\no.\nName of\nCountry\nNumber of persons \nwhom assistance was \nextended during May \n2014 to December \n2017 \nDomicile of individual\n1 Afghanistan 184 Maharashtra, West Bengal, \nTamil Nadu,  Delhi, Haryana, Telangana, Jammu\nand Kashmir, Jharkhand\n2 Algeria 81 Bihar, Kerala, Maharashtra, Odisha, Punjab,\nRajasthan\n3 Azerbaijan 45 Tamil Nadu, Maharashtra, West Bengal, Punjab,\nKarnataka, Rajasthan\n4 Bahrain 403 Maharashtra, Andhra Pradesh, Telangana,\nRajasthan, Delhi, Gujarat, Kerala\n5 Belarus 7 Punjab, Uttarakhand, Bihar\n6 Bangladesh 33 West Bengal, Andhra Pradesh, Delhi , Assam,\nBihar, Uttar Pradesh\n7 Brazil 1 Tamil Nadu\n8 Brunei 3 Kerala\n9 Cambodia 19 Kerala, Punjab, Tamil Nadu, West Bengal, Bihar,\nUttarakhand, Uttar Pradesh\n10 Canada 4 Uttar Pradesh, Maharashtra, Bihar\n11 China 47 Kerala, Punjab, Andhra Pradesh, Uttar Pradesh,\nGujarat, Rajasthan\n12 Colombia 14 Kerala, Uttar Pradesh, Punjab, Delhi, Haryana,\nRajasthan\n13 Congo 1 Andhra Pradesh \n14 Cote D’ Ivoire 7 Hyderabad, T